#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:1
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:3
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:6
msgid ""
"Interface to access objects in bulk. It provides local access to previously "
"fetched objects and helps improve performance by reducing round-trip calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:8
msgid ""
"Assistive technology should do a bulk query of all the objects in a new "
"window with the `GetItems` method, and then update them dynamically with the "
"`AddAccessible` and `RemoveAccessible` signals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:10
msgid ""
"<!---\n"
"Original description: \n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The application should expose this interface at the\n"
"/org/a11y/atspi/cache object path.\n"
"\n"
"The `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` interface has method to transfer an "
"object\\'s D-Bus id. The\n"
"caller has to then query the object\\'s properties individually.\n"
"Transferring objects one by one and then their properties produces a lot\n"
"of traffic in the accessibility bus.\n"
"\n"
"So, this Cache interface can be used to query objects in bulk. Assistive\n"
"tech should try to do a bulk query of all the objects in a new window\n"
"with the GetItems method, and then update them dynamically from the\n"
"AddAccessible and RemoveAccessible signals.\n"
"\n"
"FIXME: Does GetItems only get called if an application implements\n"
"GetApplicationBusAddress? GTK4 doesn\\'t implement that, but it\n"
"implements GetItems -does that ever get called?\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:32
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:34
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Cache.GetItems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:38
msgid ""
"GetItems (\n"
"  OUT nodes a((so)(so)(so)iiassusau)\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:42
msgid ""
"Returns a list of cached accessible objects as an array with one element for "
"each available object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:44
msgid "Each element in the array contains the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:46
msgid ""
"(so): accessible object reference - D-Bus name and object path. The rest of "
"the fields refer to this main object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:49
msgid ""
"(so): application reference - D-Bus name and object path. This is the owner "
"of the main object; the root path of the application that registered via the "
"Embed method of the org.a11y.atspi.Socket interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:54
msgid "(so): parent object reference - D-Bus name and object path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:56
msgid "If the main object has no parent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:58
msgid "If it is a control, or a window, return the parent application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:60
msgid ""
"If the object has the application role, return a null reference. FIXME: atk-"
"adaptor/adaptors/cache-adaptor.c:append_cache_item() returns a reference to "
"the registry in this case (the one it obtained from the initial "
"Socket::Embed call); GTK4 returns a null reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:66
msgid ""
"Otherwise, return a null reference (\\\"\\\" for the application name name "
"and \\\"/org/a11y/atspi/null\\\" for the object path)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:69
msgid ""
"i: index in parent, or -1 for transient widgets/menu items. Equivalent to "
"the GetIndexInParent method of the ` org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:73
msgid ""
"i: child count of main object, or -1 for defunct/menus. Equivalent to the "
"ChildCount property of the `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:77
msgid ""
"as: array of names of the interfaces that the main object supports. "
"Equivalent to the GetInterfaces method of the org.a11y.atspi.Accessible "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:81
msgid ""
"s: human-readable, localized, short name for the main object. Equivalent to "
"the Name property of the `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:85
msgid ""
"u: role. Equivalent to the GetRole method of the `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:88
msgid ""
"s: human-readable, localized description of the object in more detail. "
"Equivalent to the Description property of the `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:92
msgid ""
"au: Set of states currently held by an object. Equivalent to the GetState "
"method of the `org.a11y.atspi.Accessible` interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:95
msgid ""
"<!---\n"
"Part of the original description: \n"
"\n"
"Deprecation note: The signature for the return value of this method\n"
"changed in 2015, in commit b2c8c4c7. It used to be\n"
"\\\"a((so)(so)(so)a(so)assusau)\\\". The \\\"a(so)\\\" instead of \\\"ii\\\" "
"is a\n"
"list of references to child objects. The implementation in atspi-misc.c\n"
"can handle either version, although the intention is to deprecate the\n"
"code that handles the old version. Qt still uses this old signature and\n"
"should be changed to the new scheme (see qspi_struct_marshallers.cpp in\n"
"the Qt source code).\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:109
msgid "Signals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:111
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Cache::AddAccessible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:115
msgid ""
"AddAccessible (\n"
"  nodeAdded ((so)(so)(so)iiassusau)\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:119
msgid ""
"Add an accessible object to the cache. See the "
"`org.a11y.atspi.Cache.GetItems` for a description of the signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:122
msgid "org.a11y.atspi.Cache::RemoveAccessible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:126
msgid ""
"RemoveAccessible (\n"
"  nodeRemoved (so)\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/dbus/org.a11y.atspi.Cache.md:130
msgid "Remove an accessible object from the cache."
msgstr ""
